From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000_linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 23:24:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gnulib: use GNU nodiscard attribute on GCC 15

GCC 15 accepts the C23 nodiscard spelling but GNU m4 1.4.19's bundled
gnulib headers place the macro between "static inline" and the return
type. That placement is valid for GNU __attribute__((warn_unused_result))
but not for the C23 attribute spelling, so host-m4 fails to build.

The same old gnulib snapshot also forces _FORTIFY_SOURCE on, which
conflicts with Alpine/musl's fortify headers and its replacement cdefs.h.

Keep using the GNU nodiscard attribute form and leave fortify to the host
toolchain.
---
 lib/config.hin | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/config.hin b/lib/config.hin
index 12e3e704c..e9e57a6c3 100644
--- a/lib/config.hin
+++ b/lib/config.hin
@@ -195,7 +195,7 @@
 
 /* Enable compile-time and run-time bounds-checking, and some warnings,
       without upsetting newer glibc. */
-   #if defined __OPTIMIZE__ && __OPTIMIZE__
+   #if 0
    # define _FORTIFY_SOURCE 2
    #endif
   
@@ -2584,7 +2584,7 @@
 # define _GL_ATTRIBUTE_MALLOC
 #endif
 
-#if 201710L < __STDC_VERSION__
+#if 0
 # define _GL_ATTRIBUTE_NODISCARD [[__nodiscard__]]
 #elif _GL_HAS_ATTRIBUTE (warn_unused_result)
 # define _GL_ATTRIBUTE_NODISCARD __attribute__ ((__warn_unused_result__))
-- 
2.50.0
